From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:54:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/66] qualcommax: ipq807x: c-360: light the radio LEDs

The 2.4, 5 and 5/6 LEDs had no trigger. Phy numbers follow the order
the radios were first found in, and they differ between units: one
C-360 has its two cards at phy2 and phy3, another at phy3 and phy4. So
board.d cannot name them. A hotplug script ties each LED to its radio
by device path instead, with the radio's phyNradio trigger: the LED is
lit while the radio is enabled. The card on pcie1 has no LED.

Tested on a unit: the three LEDs follow the IPQ8074's two radios and
the 6 GHz card.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 .../hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-360-leds  | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-360-leds

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-360-leds b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-360-leds
new file mode 100755
index 0000000000..66f33cbdc6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-360-leds
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Arista C-360: each radio LED follows its radio, found by device path.
+# Phy numbers follow the order the radios were first found in, which
+# differs between units. 2.4 and 5 are the IPQ8074's radios, 5/6 is the
+# 6 GHz card on pcie0; the card on pcie1 has no LED. "phyNradio" lights
+# the LED while the radio is enabled.
+
+[ "$ACTION" = add ] || exit 0
+
+. /lib/functions.sh
+
+[ "$(board_name)" = arista,c-360 ] || exit 0
+
+case "$(readlink "/sys/class/ieee80211/$DEVICENAME/device")" in
+*/c000000.wifi)
+	if iw phy "$DEVICENAME" info | grep -q "Band 1:"; then
+		led=green:wlan-2ghz
+	else
+		led=green:wlan-5ghz
+	fi
+	;;
+*/0000:01:00.0)
+	led=green:wlan-6ghz
+	;;
+*)
+	exit 0
+	;;
+esac
+
+echo "${DEVICENAME}radio" > "/sys/class/leds/$led/trigger"
